NAME
     strace - what system calls a program makes

SYNOPSIS
     strace [-f] [-c] [-T] [-s N] [-e NAME,...] COMMAND [ARG...]
     strace -p PID

DESCRIPTION
     strace runs COMMAND and prints every system call it makes with its
     arguments and its result, or attaches to a process that is already
     running. It is the ptrace interface underneath, so a process can
     only be traced by whoever may signal it.

OPTIONS
     -f              follow children
     -c              count them instead of printing each one
     -T              print how long each call took
     -s N            print at most N bytes of each string
     -e NAME,...     only these calls
     -p PID          attach to a running process

SEE ALSO
     ps(1), dmesg(1)
